A||||11||sqoach||What the !?!?!?||||11||
Z||000000||sqoach||04-25-2001||03:18 PM||||Ok, so I go out to my car to check on some stuff. Decided to go ahead and check the computer for any codes. Nope, all is good. (Which is weird because last time I checked, I had a code 34) Then I notice this weird noise coming from the engine somewhere. My little paperclip is still in the computer thingy, so I took it out and the noise stopped. Put it back in, and there's that weird noise again. It's coming from this connector thing (IAC???) right by the TBI. It has four wires going to it. Is it suppose to make a noise? I thought I had screwed something up but I guess it's ok.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||11
Z||000001||Hank is Here||04-25-2001||03:26 PM||||I thought that when you got codes it was not supposed to be running?    ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||04-25-2001||03:32 PM||||To get the codes you put the key in the on position and check them that way. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||04-25-2001||03:39 PM||||key was on, car not running||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||04-25-2001||03:46 PM||||If I remember right, the fan on my car runs when I read the codes.  Not sure thats exactly what it was, but I know something runs and makes noise.  It may be a diagnostic mode for whatever is making the noise.||||reg||1
Z||000005||NSUMEY||04-25-2001||04:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B>Ok, so I go out to my car to check on some stuff. Decided to go ahead and check the computer for any codes. Nope, all is good. (Which is weird because last time I checked, I had a code 34) Then I notice this weird noise coming from the engine somewhere. My little paperclip is still in the computer thingy, so I took it out and the noise stopped. Put it back in, and there's that weird noise again. It's coming from this connector thing (IAC???) right by the TBI. It has four wires going to it. Is it suppose to make a noise? I thought I had screwed something up but I guess it's ok.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>when you jumper the ALDL (computer thingy) it puts the vehicle into diagnostic mode...then it cycles all the solenoids off and on to make sure everything is up to par..so YES it is normal......||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dave Gunsul||04-25-2001||08:15 PM||||No, when you check the codes with a jumper<BR>it also resets the IAC. (idle air control)<BR>It also runs the trunk fan.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000007||jaguiler||04-25-2001||08:36 PM||||what trunk fan?<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000008||c m west||04-25-2001||08:45 PM||||what you heard was the motor inside the IAC reseting itself, it does this everytime the computer is put into diagnostic mode while diagnosing a code or codes relating to idle or EGR issues - its common, natural, and supposed to happen, so no worries<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||04-25-2001||09:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jaguiler:<BR><B>what trunk fan?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The V6 Cars have a blower in the trunk that blows air on the alternator and coil.  It comes on when the radiator fan comes on.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000010||sqoach||04-25-2001||11:29 PM||||Well that's good to know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I thought I might be having <I>more</I> problems. Thanks guys.||||reg||10
Z||000011||LZeitgeist||04-26-2001||01:07 PM||||DJRice - <P>Only the V6 cars up to and including '87... the '88's don't have the fan in back.||||reg||1
